<p>I just can't take this seriously. We've had&#8230; two, if I can remember correctly, SCPs that play strongly on the body horror of being infected by bees or wasps, but you spend virtually no time cultivating the necessary sense of disgust for that to work. You have some implications that things are getting weirder (bodies/DNA/offspring changing), but only implications, and they're lightly sprinkled through a sea of bland exposition, bland expository dialogue, and difficult-to-believe plot turns.</p>
<p>- Like, having your characters point out how ridiculous it is to wear bee suits all the time just made me go, &quot;Yeah, that's dumb, why did you write that?&quot;<br />
- Also it's odd that you dedicated a huge table to flowers and <em>nothing</em> to the crazier (body/identity horror) stuff.<br />
- Another example, you log is full of a: a few items of actual necessary plot + a whole lot of nothing + One body horror reference + Bear friggin Bond-villain level monologue-ing exposition. The O5 logs similarly lacked unique voices or interesting content.</p>
<p>I'm guessing a lot of this could be due to this being a contest entry. I haven't read the other articles, and this didn't really make me want to click any of the crosslinks.</p>
<p>My biggest takeaway, you've got a base/starting SCP that still feels like it needs some polish before making the mainlist (in terms of how and when effects are discussed), but you're also asking it to support an end-of-the-world story that often beggars suspension of disbelief and is weighed down with dry story mechanisms. That ship doesn't float.</p>
<p>-1</p>

							</div>

								
					
