			<div class="content" id="post-content-3845587">
									

<p>While I do have to agree with some of the criticisms proposed by the users above, I ultimately found this story to be engaging throughout most of the read. Like, the O5 correspondences for instance. I found those mostly unnecessary due to the large volume of things the Overseers spoke about, but I ultimately enjoyed them because we don't often see how the O5 will go through and deal with such an anomaly in its various stages.</p>
<p>The way this scip built on itself throughout was insane, even if some parts felt like a cheesy action flick (the initial raid on the Chaos Insurgency outpost, for instance). You took the time to explore nearly every avenue this scip offered, even if some parts weren't particularly interesting, and I find it commendable.</p>
<p>One final thing: I was pretty ambivalent about the final note. It seems more like a place to cram in bee references than a necessary addition to the story. I'd say the parts that pertain directly to O5-2 and MTF-Mu-Pi-6 are the most in need of work. The rest is enjoyable.</p>
<p>+1</p>

